    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d154-a1-a1">

                <pb facs="0164" n="90" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg90"/>

                <head>Mr. Cartier to Viscount Monck</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crown Law Department,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Quebec,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-02-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 28, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The undersigned has the honor, in addition to his report of the 24th ultimo, to
                    transmit to his excellency the governor general copy of a letter, with
                    enclosure, received from the collector of customs at Montreal, in relation to
                    two vessels, Almandares and Pinero, the former of which is reported as having
                    been sold to Spanish subjects at Havana, and. the latter, still lying in the
                    Lachine canal, as having been transferred by bill of sale to a gentleman
                    residing In the city of Montreal.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEORGE E. CARTIER.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Attorney General</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">L.
                            C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
